meta {
  name: search
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/shows/search?title=severance&nbpp=20&order=popularity
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  title: severance
  nbpp: 20
  order: popularity
  ~summary: true
  ~recent: true
  ~page: 1
}

headers {
  X-BetaSeries-Key: {{apiKey}}
  X-BetaSeries-Version: 3.0
  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
}

docs {
  Search the catalog by title, with member information when a token is sent.

  Backs Client.search_shows(). No example block yet: the response has not been
  captured against a real key, so the parsing in client.py assumes this
  endpoint returns the same show objects as /shows/display (verified there:
  in_account, creation, status, platforms.svods[].name, notes.mean, slug).
  Run this request, save the response as an example, and correct the parsing
  if any of those five fields turns out to be absent here.

  `summary` is left disabled on purpose: it returns "only essential series
  info", which is likely to drop exactly those fields.
}
